# Scaling — add one thing only when it breaks

Today: Vercel (already runs many instances behind its own load balancer) + one Supabase Postgres. That is enough for the spec's 100 concurrent users and thousands of members. Do not skip steps.

| Symptom | Check first (free) | Then add | Cost we accept |
|---|---|---|---|
| Slow queries, DB CPU high | Missing index, `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` | Bigger Supabase compute | Money |
| "Too many connections" at a spike | Direct Postgres clients in serverless code | Supavisor **transaction** pooler (port 6543) | No session-level features / prepared statements |
| Reads still saturate the DB | Indexes + bigger compute done? | Read replica for A5 search and profile views | Replication lag |
| Same expensive read repeated | Is it really hot? | `'use cache'` + `cacheTag`; on write, `updateTag` (Server Action, read-your-writes) or `revalidateTag(tag, profile)` | Stale until revalidated |
| User waits on slow side work | Is it needed before the response? | `after()`; if it must retry → Supabase Queues (pgmq) | "Done" means queued, not finished |
| Data too big for one machine | Not in sight | Sharding by `community_id` | Cross-shard queries (already forbidden: no cross-community search) |

## May be stale vs. never stale (product decision)

- **Cacheable:** community field defs (G1, profiles), community start page AA, group info text.
- **Never cached, never read from a replica:** messages, unread, membership, roles, block list, private notes/ratings, album access, verification status. You must see your own message and your own admission immediately.
- Never put user-specific data under a shared cache key — that leaks one member's data to another.

## Stateless servers

Instances are many and short-lived. No sessions, maps, rate limits, or caches in module-level memory. State lives in Supabase (DB, Auth cookies, Storage).

## Not now

Redis, BullMQ, NGINX / own load balancer, microservices, read replicas, sharding. Supabase Auth is already stateless, so a session store is not needed. Before launch, check the Supabase plan's DB connection and Realtime connection quotas (one socket per client).
